title: ZinniaInitialIntroduction
---
<<if !has_npc_been_contacted("HospitableFlora")>>
    Zinnia: Well hello, human! Have you come to bask in the healing waters of these springs?
    Zinnia: Come, come. I am called Zinnia by humans. I shan't bite or sting. Aren't you quite the ravishing specimen.
    <<make_contact_with_npc "HospitableFlora">>
    <<jump QuestionsForZinniaSwitch>>
<<else>>
    Zinnia: Marvelous to see you still alive, dear. [Needles you playfully]
    <<jump QuestionsForZinniaSwitch>>
<<endif>>
===

title: QuestionsForZinniaSwitch
---
-> I'm surprised to be communicating with you like this, mind to mind. I have encountered only hostile members of your kind.
    <<jump ZinniaExplainsOurFirstQuestion>>
-> You've met other humans? And communicated with them telepathically?
    <<jump ZinnaAndOtherHumans>>
-> I should go. 
===

title: ZinniaExplainsOurFirstQuestion
---
Zinnia: I do hope you were not harmed. Come, enter the spring water and be infused and healed of your blights.

===

title: ZinniaExplainsOurFirstQuestion_QA
---
-> I'm alive. Why are they hostile and not you?
    Zinnia: My sisters have been dealt a terrible fate. They are sick, you see. A blight created by the Kin long ago, and it makes them violent to all but Kin.
    Zinnia: I have yet never succumbed. These springs seem to be a natural innoculation. They draw from deep waters, you see.
    <<jump ZinniaExplainsOurFirstQuestion_QA>>
-> I had other questions.
    <<jump QuestionsForZinniaSwitch>>
-> Have you tried using the water to heal them?
    <<jump ZinniaTalksAboutHealingSisters>>
-> So, all of you are sentient?
    <<jump ZinniaIsSentient>>
-> I should go.
===

title: ZinnaAndOtherHumans
---
Zinnia: Truth be told, you are but the second human I could communicate with, but the other... she was a friend to me. She gave me that name.
===

title: ZinniaTalksAboutHealingSisters
---
Zinnia: Yes. Alas the water is innoculation, but not cure. But I have not been idle. I have been working on a treatment.
Zinnia: However, I cannot leave these hotsprings. I'd get sick myself before I could help them. 
// -> Maybe I could help.
//     <<jump ZinniaPlayerAsksIfCanHelp>>
-> That's too bad. 
=== 

title: ZinniaPlayerAsksIfCanHelp
---
Zinnia: Hmm, yes it could work. Your modifications by the Kin... I could adapt the gene tonic for human use. You'd have to inject it intravenously.
Zinnia: It might even work. The ability first placates the subject, then, I am hoping, actually cures the blight.
-> Uh, I'll have to think about just injecting your tonic. Is it even safe?
    Zinnia: I have no idea! But it would be very interesting to see what happens and it could do much good.
    -> Ok, I'll give it a try.
        <<jump ZinniaPlayerAgreesToGiveATry>>
    -> I don't think it's a good idea.
-> Ok, I'll give it a try.
    <<jump ZinniaPlayerAgreesToGiveATry>>
===

title: ZinniaPlayerAgreesToGiveATry
---
Zinnia: Ok, I unlocked the shed door, right over there. I think you'll be fine. And keep a note of side effects, will you?
<<unlock_door "ZinniaShedDoor">>
Zinnia: Oh, I can't wait! Go. Do this for me, and I'll find a way to reward you. We Florites can be formidable allies.
===

title: ZinniaIsSentient
---
Zinnia: Aye. We were in these caves before the Kin ever delved and descended, having destroyed the surface.
Zinnia: They came down and continue in their destructive behavior. They invented the blight. See us as pests, they do.
Zinnia: We used to be peaceful. Those of us unaffected still are.
<<jump QuestionsForZinniaSwitch>>
===